s-v-state/\" aria-description=\"Citation for case: Williams v. State\">773 S. W. 2d 525</a></span>; No. 89-5110, <span class=\"citation\" data-id=\"1495552\"><a href=\"/opinion/1495552/lingar-v-state/\" aria-description=\"Citation for case: Lingar v. State\">766 S. W. 2d 640</a></span>; No. 89-5193, <span class=\"citation\" data-id=\"1750509\"><a href=\"/opinion/1750509/kennedy-v-state/\" aria-description=\"Citation for case: Kennedy v. State\">545 So. 2d 214</a></span>; No. 89-5245, <span class=\"citation\" data-id=\"524119\"><a href=\"/opinion/524119/arthur-james-julius-v-charlie-jones-warden-holman-unit/\" aria-description=\"Citation for case: Arthur James Julius v. Charlie Jones, Warden, Holman Unit\">875 F. 2d 1520</a></span>; No. 89-5256, <span class=\"citation\" data-id=\"1624931\"><a href=\"/opinion/1624931/guinan-v-state/\" aria-description=\"Citation for case: Guinan v. State\">769 S. W. 2d 427</a></span>; No. 89-5442, <span class=\"citation\" data-id=\"522194\"><a href=\"/opinion/522194/carlos-deluna-v-james-a-lynaugh-director-texas-department-of/\" aria-description=\"Citation for case: Carlos Deluna v. James A. Lynaugh, Director, Texas...\">873 F. 2d 757</a></span>; No. 89-5496, <span class=\"citation\" data-id=\"1737402\"><a href=\"/opinion/1737402/cochran-v-state/\" aria-description=\"Citation for case: Cochran v. State\">548 So. 2d 1062</a></span>.</p>\n</opinion>"},{"id":9085794,"type":"dissent","typeCode":"040dissent","perCuriam":false,"author":"Brennanmarshall","joinedBy":"","pageCount":null,"textLength":597,"isHtml":true,"text":"<opinion type=\"dissent\">\n<author id=\"b838-12\">Justice Brennan and Justice Marshall,</author>\n<p id=\"AvnN\">dissenting.</p>\n<p id=\"b838-13\">Adhering to our views that the death penalty is in all circumstances cruel and unusual punishment prohibited by the Eighth and Fourteenth Amendments, <em>Gregg </em>v. <em>Georgia, </em><span class=\"citation\" data-id=\"9426555\"><a href=\"/opinion/109532/gregg-v-georgia/#227\" aria-description=\"Citation for case: Gregg v. Georgia\">428 U. S. 153, 227, 231</a></span> (1976), we would grant certiorari and vacate the death sentences in these cases.</p>\n</opinion>"}],"citations":[]}